        "## Question 12\n",
        "\n",
        "Create an array and demonstrate the difference between a slice/view and a copy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "81816a88",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "81816a88"
      },
      "source": [
        "Theory: A slice is usually a view into the original array, so changing it can change the original. copy() creates independent data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 12,
      "id": "b47b9d71",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "b47b9d71",
        "outputId": "4ad6c662-93c9-47e2-c534-03245aa8f1dd"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Original after changing view: [ 10 999  30  40  50]\n",
            "View: [999  30  40]\n",
            "Original after changing copy: [ 10 999  30  40  50]\n",
            "Copy: [ 20 777  40]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "original = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])\n",
        "view = original[1:4]\n",
        "copy = original[1:4].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "view[0] = 999\n",
        "print(\"Original after changing view:\", original)\n",
        "print(\"View:\", view)\n",
        "\n",
        "copy[1] = 777\n",
        "print(\"Original after changing copy:\", original)\n",
        "print(\"Copy:\", copy)"
      ]
    },
